+# Migration instructions
+
+Read the migration tracker and stage report in VeloraMCDev/docs before changing code.
+Use this checkout directly; do not create a worktree unless the user requests one.
+Do not erase existing behavior or rename persisted IDs, database paths, volume names,
+Minecraft protocol identities or updater/signing identities without compatibility tests.
+Keep shared gameplay and SMP/Frontiers implementations out of public repositories.
+Public builds must resolve no private dependency. Do not import mixed legacy files
+wholesale. Preserve source revision, checksums and attribution for each extraction.
+Do not claim a placeholder is runnable. Record validation and incomplete tasks honestly.
+Use generic, synthetic examples; never commit credentials, player data or operator URLs.
+MIT applies to platform code; artwork/trademark/private distribution terms are separate.
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ccaaf93
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# Velora experiences
+
+**Velora owns the platform. Each instance owns the experience.**
+
+Responsibility: Private gameplay modules and individual SMP/Frontiers experiences.
+
+## Migration status
+
+Stage 1 foundation branch. Application/gameplay extraction has not started; this is a repository foundation, not a deployable product.
+The existing SCOPENET-MC installation remains the functional implementation.
+Source baseline: `scopeddlol/SCOPENET-MC@57daa92cb6cb4027982d06bfa1c692ab9edb88ff` (includes the Docker temporary-directory fix).
+
+The task tracker and stage report live in [Velora docs](https://github.com/VeloraMCDev/docs/tree/codex/stage-1-foundation/migration).
+Seven platform repositories are intended to be public under MIT. Experiences and
+shared gameplay remain private; no public package may require them to build or boot.
+Repository visibility has not been changed by this branch.
+
+## Next boundary
+
+Verify private repository visibility and approved distribution terms before importing gameplay source or assets. This repository has no MIT grant.
